  "document": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>The Last Lighthouse Keeper</title>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The Last Lighthouse Keeper\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"On a rock off the Hebrides, the final keeper hands over the lamp.\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://magazine.example.com/features/the-last-lighthouse\"></head>\n<body><article class=\"longform\">\n<h1>The Last Lighthouse Keeper</h1>\n<p class=\"standfirst\">On a rock off the Hebrides, the final keeper hands over the lamp.</p>\n<figure><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/i/lamp-480.webp 480w, /i/lamp-960.webp 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 480px, 960px\"><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/i/lamp-480.jpg 480w, /i/lamp-960.jpg 960w\"><img src=\"/i/lamp-960.jpg\" alt=\"The lamp room\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"960\" height=\"640\"></picture><figcaption>The lamp room at dusk.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The boat comes on Thursdays, weather permitting. Morag has learned not to count on it. She keeps a ledger of the days it did not come, and the ledger is longer than she likes to admit.</p>\n<img class=\"lazy\" data-src=\"/i/rock.jpg\" data-srcset=\"/i/rock-480.jpg 480w, /i/rock-960.jpg 960w\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAAAACH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw==\" alt=\"The rock from the sea\">\n<noscript><img src=\"/i/rock.jpg\" alt=\"The rock from the sea\"></noscript>\n<p>Automation arrived in 1998. The lamp turns by itself now, and a sensor reports fog to a station on the mainland. The keepers were pensioned off one by one.</p>\n<img src=\"https://magazine.example.com/pixel.gif\" width=\"1\" height=\"1\" alt=\"\">\n<img src=\"/i/diagram.svg\" alt=\"Lens diagram\" width=\"320\" height=\"200\">\n<p>What remains is the part no sensor reports: the smell of paraffin that never left the stairwell, the handwriting in the logbooks, the way the wind sounds in the gallery rail.</p>\n<img srcset=\"/i/small.jpg 1x, /i/large.jpg 2x\" src=\"/i/small.jpg\" alt=\"Handwriting in a logbook\">\n</article></body></html>\n",
